[["page","lines",0],{"text":"Page 5 of 14Oberoi et al. BMC Medical Research Methodology (2022) 22:64","fontSize":8,"x":56.692901611,"y":31.332613769999966,"width":481.89060107399996,"height":8.516967773000033}]
[["page","lines",1],{"text":"Table 1 Quotes from oncology providers","fontSize":9,"x":56.692901611,"y":86.33261376999997,"width":149.5071,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",2],{"text":"b. Study is inclusive in nature 1.1b “The recruitment methods I think are inclusive for basically captur-","fontSize":8,"x":164.317306518,"y":105.290987793,"width":365.71999315999994,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",3],{"text":"ing any patient that may be interested in the study because this is also","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":114.290987793,"width":209.89200000000005,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",4],{"text":"through nurse practitioner and so I think the – I think it’s inclusive of all","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":123.290987793,"width":211.0680000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",5],{"text":"patients who – no matter what they’ve gone through in terms of treat-","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":132.290987793,"width":211.8199999984721,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",6],{"text":"ment: ‑","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":141.290987793,"width":21.72800000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",7],{"text":"Participant 5, medical oncologist, tertiary cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":150.290987793,"width":174.87759999847208,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",8],{"text":"c. Simplicity of the methods 1.1c “And I guess what appeals to me is that you seem to have a simplified","fontSize":8,"x":164.31730651800004,"y":162.386987793,"width":374.98079999999993,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",9],{"text":"recruitment process so that it won’t take a lot of our time”. Participant 6,","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":171.386987793,"width":214.8456000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",10],{"text":"med onco, regional","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":180.386987793,"width":61.88720000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",11],{"text":"1.2c “I mean yeah, I mean the fact that we can email you guys the contact","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":189.386987793,"width":221.79599999999994,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",12],{"text":"information, you’ll take care of the rest, that’s just – it’s great.” Participant","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":198.386987793,"width":216.33999999083198,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",13],{"text":"P8, medical oncologist, tertiary cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530651800004,"y":207.386987793,"width":142.97360000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",14],{"text":"2. Barriers","fontSize":8,"x":56.693308230000014,"y":219.482987793,"width":30.447199999999995,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",15],{"text":"Health system barriers","fontSize":8,"x":56.693308230000014,"y":228.482987793,"width":70.63039999999998,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",16],{"text":"a. Coordination between discharging clinicians 2.1 a “Having an awareness of – for example between clinical and nursing","fontSize":8,"x":164.31730823,"y":219.482987793,"width":374.49280000152794,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",17],{"text":"and us, when they are booking their discharge, they could put the sheet","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":228.482987793,"width":213.82880000152807,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",18],{"text":"on there”. Participant 5, medical oncologist, tertiary cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":237.482987793,"width":204.10080000000016,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",19],{"text":"2.2a “The offer needs to be made in the clinic by myself and the nurse","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":246.482987793,"width":205.65279999999984,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",20],{"text":"that’s working with me in the follow-up clinic.”Participant4, Radiation","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":255.482987793,"width":209.7015999969442,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",21],{"text":"oncologist, tertiary cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":264.482987793,"width":104.8064,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",22],{"text":"2.3 a “It’ll be easy for the ones that don’t get radiation or don’t need radia-","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":273.482987793,"width":219.31600001220795,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",23],{"text":"tion, they just see us and if they come back in like three months or two","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":282.482987793,"width":209.11599999999999,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",24],{"text":"months to make sure you’re doing okay on the hormonal therapy and","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":291.482987793,"width":209.29279999999994,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",25],{"text":"then I discharge them, those will be straightforward” Participant 2, medi‑","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":300.482987793,"width":220.092799996944,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",26],{"text":"cal oncologist, regional cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":309.482987793,"width":118.67039999999997,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",27],{"text":"2.4a “Whoever is the last to see or treat, so it often falls on the radiation –","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":318.482987793,"width":216.52400000152807,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",28],{"text":"patients undergoing radiation, it will often fall to the radiation oncologist","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":327.482987793,"width":219.68399999999997,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",29],{"text":"to discharge. Often it’s just through the chart that, you know, I’ll see my","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":336.482987793,"width":211.5567999908401,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",30],{"text":"patients for the last time for me and I see that radiation oncology still has","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":345.482987793,"width":218.9960000030561,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",31],{"text":"an appointment down the line so I could certainly in my last note on the","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":354.482987793,"width":216.54960000000005,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",32],{"text":"patient indicate that they’d be a good candidate and even write that in","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":363.482987793,"width":212.9480000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",33],{"text":"the chart.” Participant 6, medical oncologist, regional cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":372.482987793,"width":210.3167999984721,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",34],{"text":"b. Time constraints for clinicians 2.1b “So, for me, it’s – for the time sometimes, it’s just in some cases,","fontSize":8,"x":164.31730823,"y":384.578987793,"width":353.396000001528,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",35],{"text":"because I am the sole oncologist here in these areas. So, it’s just sometimes","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":393.578987793,"width":222.02080000152796,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",36],{"text":"I get too busy and might not have always the time to discuss that.” Partici‑","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":402.578987793,"width":221.3584000015278,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",37],{"text":"pant 7, medical oncologist, regional cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":411.578987793,"width":158.73360000000008,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",38],{"text":"2.2b You can prepare as best you can but if you have a very busy clinic","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":420.578987793,"width":209.9487999999999,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",39],{"text":"talking about trials, interventions, studies does take more time and it can","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":429.578987793,"width":217.84399999694415,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",40],{"text":"fall into the backseat if you will”. Participant 12, medical oncologist,","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":438.578987793,"width":206.06879999847217,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",41],{"text":"tertiary cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":447.578987793,"width":67.92719999694407,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",42],{"text":"Patient related barriers 2.1 c “And that’s the only thing is that lots of my patients may be able to","fontSize":8,"x":56.693309941999985,"y":459.674987793,"width":475.343198288,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",43],{"text":"speak English but they may not be written-language literate so for them","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":468.674987793,"width":215.796000006104,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",44],{"text":"they may find some barrier to understanding the information that they","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":477.674987793,"width":213.1952,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",45],{"text":"would be given but they are obviously not going to be eligible” Participant","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":486.674987793,"width":221.74240000000032,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",46],{"text":"7, medical oncologist, regional cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":495.674987793,"width":142.1744,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",47],{"text":"2.2c “They might work for some but like most of them like mails rather","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":504.674987793,"width":208.788800001528,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",48],{"text":"than email. The only issue like the response rates, I am not sure about the","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":513.674987793,"width":217.45280000000002,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",49],{"text":"response rate.” Participant 2, medical oncologist, regional cancer centre","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":522.674987793,"width":221.98880000152803,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",50],{"text":"2.3c “You know obviously I will expect the uptake to be lower than those","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":531.674987793,"width":215.01360000152795,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",51],{"text":"who receive phone call directly from the program; some of them are","fontSize":8,"x":317.08530823,"y":540.674987793,"width":203.21200000152794,"height":8}]
